menu "System metrics"
    config SYSTEM_METRICS_TASK_STATS_ENABLED
        bool "Enable per-task CPU usage / priority / stack metrics (debug only)"
        depends on ESP_OPENTELEMETRY_METRICS_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Collects dust_mite_task_cpu_usage, dust_mite_task_priority and
            dust_mite_task_stack_min_free_bytes via FreeRTOS
            uxTaskGetSystemState(). FreeRTOS documents this whole API
            family as debug-only, not for production use. On a dual-core
            ESP-IDF build it holds the kernel lock, with interrupts masked,
            while it walks every task and scans its stack for the high-water
            mark, so interrupts on both cores wait for each refresh - leave
            disabled unless actively debugging task scheduling/CPU usage.

    config SYSTEM_METRICS_TASK_STATS_REFRESH_MS
        int "Task stats refresh interval (ms)"
        depends on SYSTEM_METRICS_TASK_STATS_ENABLED
        range 100 3600000
        default 10000
        help
            How often the task stats are read again. Collections in between
            report the last read, so a short interval gives finer CPU usage
            and masks interrupts more often.

    config SYSTEM_METRICS_LARGEST_FREE_BLOCK_ENABLED
        bool "Enable largest free heap block metric (debug only)"
        depends on ESP_OPENTELEMETRY_METRICS_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Collects dust_mite_largest_free_block_bytes via
            heap_caps_get_largest_free_block(MALLOC_CAP_8BIT), which walks
            every allocated and free block (via tlsf_walk_pool()) under a
            heap lock, for both the internal SRAM heap and the PSRAM heap.
            The PSRAM walk requires real SPI reads of PSRAM-resident TLSF
            metadata, which competes with the camera's own PSRAM DMA traffic
            at the hardware bus level - independent of CPU core or task
            priority. On this board it disrupts the camera's real-time JPEG
            frame capture during streaming (issue #43) - leave disabled
            unless actively debugging heap fragmentation, and disable again
            afterward.
endmenu
